From a4148f42749d3a11b628de36af63ecf896f94026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomer Sagi <ts.tomersagi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:58:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Pin dependencies in requirements.lock and apply security
 bumps

- Add requirements.lock: the server's pip freeze (2026-11-04) re-resolved
  for Python 3.10 with security fixes: pillow 12.3.0, urllib3 2.8.0,
  sqlparse 0.6.0, requests 2.33.0, certifi 2026.10.18, idna 3.15,
  sentry-sdk 1.45.1, simpleeval 1.0.5. Unused packages that were only in
  the server venv (Flask, Werkzeug, Jinja2, lxml, qlever, ...) are gone.
- Move the remaining old-client imports to elasticsearch7 and drop
  elasticsearch==7.8.1 (it pinned urllib3 to 1.x). elasticsearch7 -> 7.17.13.
- Remove req.txt, a stale 2022 freeze that produced most Dependabot alerts.
- Document rebuilding the server venv from the lock (with rollback).

Still open (need Django 4.2 / Python 3.11): Django, DRF, django-tinymce,
Celery, django-celery-results, and Pillow 13 (needs Python >= 3.11).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TbA4CjcVjNQGFpdMRC6zTK
